# tests/llm-step, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. Durable event recording, ordered tool replay, workspace
# mutation, interjections on both sides of dispatch, and running or queued
# request interruption are all llm-step's, and all observable on the
# conversation ref. worker-common.sh curries the turns and polls.
#
# `admit_turn`/`start_turn` rather than `dispatch_turn` for the first turn: the
# pre-start interjection has to land between the admission and the dispatch,
# which is the case being tested.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/worker-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --llm-step:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --stub:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-stub --tool:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test-tool --common:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test/worker-common.sh
